* SAVE - WRITE MEMORY TO A FILE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* SAVE - WRITE MEMORY TO A FILE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:SAVE

Arms CP/M 3 SAVE, then returns to the command line so you can run a
program that loads the desired data into memory. When that program exits,
SAVE asks for an output filename and beginning/ending hexadecimal
addresses. Return at the filename prompt cancels.

This installed CP/M 3 command does NOT use the CP/M 2 SAVE pages filename
syntax. It can overwrite files after confirmation and can expose resident
data. Use only during private development on backed-up media.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
